WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.040 --> 00:00:03.300
A cooling fault needs a defined response, not a promise that a

2
00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.300
coupling cannot leak.

3
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:09.160
Detection may come from pressure, flow, temperature or other qualified monitoring.

4
00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.360
The meaning of a signal and the required action depend on the

5
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.800
configured system and approved operating process.

6
00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:18.480
The animation separates detection, containment and recovery.

7
00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:23.320
It is a conceptual response map, not a valve-operating or live-maintenance procedure.

8
00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.360
Identify which equipment is affected, which protective functions act locally, and who

9
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.700
owns the decision to isolate or reduce load.

10
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.920
An alarm clearing doesn't necessarily establish that the cause is resolved or

11
00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.540
that full operation is supported.

12
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:41.640
Verify the required restoration conditions, inspect or test as the approved procedure

13
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.580
requires, and obtain the appropriate authorization before returning to service.

14
00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.160
Preserve the event and configuration record.

15
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.220
This prevents a nominally healthy display from standing in for evidence that

16
00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:56.560
the affected mechanical, fluid, electrical and thermal interfaces are ready again.

